    {
      "id": "e24128f27c83-q19",
      "number": 19,
      "question": "In a 30 L mixture, milk: water = 3:2. How much water must be added to make the ratio 1:1?",
      "questionHtml": "In a 30 L mixture, milk: water = 3:2. How much water must be added to make the ratio 1:1?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "6 L",
          "html": "6 L"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "10 L",
          "html": "10 L"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "9 L",
          "html": "9 L"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "12 L",
          "html": "12 L"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Total parts = 3 + 2 = 5</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Milk = Total × (Milk part ÷ Total parts)</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Water = Total × (Water part ÷ Total parts)</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">For 1:1 ⇒ Final water = Milk</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">⇒ Milk = 30 × 3 ÷ 5 = 18 L</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">⇒ Water = 30 × 2 ÷ 5 = 12 L</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">⇒ Required water for 1:1 = 18 L</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">⇒ Water to add = 18 − 12 = 6 L</p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e24128f27c83-q20",
      "number": 20,
      "question": "Find the LCM of 12, 18, 30?",
      "questionHtml": "Find the LCM of 12, 18, 30?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "90",
          "html": "90"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "180",
          "html": "180"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "60",
          "html": "60"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "120",
          "html": "120"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Prime factorization of 12 = 2<span style=\"position: relative; line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> × 3</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Prime factorization of 18 = 3<span style=\"position: relative; line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> × 2</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Prime factorization of 30 = 2 × 3 × 5</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Take the highest power of all prime factors: 2<span style=\"position: relative; line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>, 3<span style=\"position: relative; line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>, 5 ⇒ LCM = 2<span style=\"position: relative; line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> × 3<span style=\"position: relative; line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> × 5 ⇒ LCM = 2 × 9 × 5 ⇒ LCM = 180</p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
